WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Ghost Deck vs Occult Deck

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.600
The Battle City Finals will finally begin.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:47.260
A battle for the God Cards and to retrieve my other self's memories.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.020
Shizuka, I can finally tell you something.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:53.910
Watch me, Shizuka.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.350
You've given me the courage to win!

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.530
But Shizuka, reality can be cruel.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.880
You should remember that.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.280
Don't avert your eyes when I easily defeat your dear brother.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.160
Say what!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.550
I won't lose, Mai!

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.820
Let me warn you, including Yugi.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.290
Don't underestimate my Amazoness Deck!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.420
Amazoness Deck?

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.930
Yugi, I haven't forgotten that I promised to duel you in this tournament.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.430
Let's have a fair fight as true duelists!

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.570
Let's find out where the finals will take place!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.220
That's the venue for the finals?

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.900
But where is that?

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.260
Is this place in the city?

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.200
I believe Kaiba Corporation is developing the land in that area.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.360
So you finally found me.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.100
How did you get into my host's mind?

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.410
I remember.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.380
Back then.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:58.120
Exactly.  I embedded my consciousness into Bakura.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.820
I have to be more careful.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.850
What happened to our promise?

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:10.330
If I help you defeat Yugi, then you'll give me the Millennium Rod.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.620
Plans have changed.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.600
What?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.260
Yugi and I are in the finals.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:24.340
If you want the Millennium Rod, then you also have to qualify for the finals.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.120
In other words, you failed.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.620
You talk tough, but you're just lame.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.460
Say whatever you want.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.630
The finals are starting soon.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.360
Try to gather the Puzzle Cards before then!

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:50.260
I'll stay inside here for a while longer.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.540
What a punk!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.610
Hey!  Are you okay, Bakura?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.350
Bakura!  Hey, Bakura!

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.600
You're awake, Bakura.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.500
You were having a nightmare.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.420
I'm fine.  Just a bad dream.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.120
I see.  Good.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.220
They did it, Bakura!

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:21.100
Yugi and Jonouchi said that they collected the Puzzle Cards!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.250
Oh, really?  That's great.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.100
Where are the finals taking place?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.900
Oops.  I forgot to ask.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:39.620
I knew Yugi would make the finals, but Jonouchi did too!

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.260
My training paid off!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.400
What are you doing?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.160
I'm going to them.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.960
No!  You need to rest!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.440
I can't waste my time here.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.460
You're...

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.910
Sleep well, geezer.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:20.770
A bloody Millennium Battle is about to begin.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.940
I don't want to be left out.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.820
Give it back!

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.840
I'm surprised there's still a lame duelist who hasn't dueled even once.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.580
I was going to keep it as a souvenir!

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:47.960
As long as I have a Puzzle Card, I'm allowed to duel.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.090
Thanks for being lame.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.620
These cards are useless.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.220
Here!

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.330
My cards!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:06.510
I heard that four duelists have collected all the Puzzle Cards.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.440
I heard six.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.370
Eight duelists make the finals.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.440
I can't waste time.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.680
Let's go check the monitor screen.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:22.180
Hey!  Do you know where I can find the remaining duelists?

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.190
What's with you?

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.740
Answer me!

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.190
- What's up?
- You wanna fight?

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:32.700
Answer me.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.530
I heard someone's dueling at the cemetery.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.360
Cemetery?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.630
There's really a duelist here?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.220
It's only a crow...  Don't scare me!

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:29.150
Leave your Duel Disk!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:35.360
Leave your Duel Disk!

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.460
It worked again!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.900
We now have five Puzzle Cards!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.810
One more to qualify for the finals.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:09:00.660
Yeah.  If one of us makes the finals, we've triumphed over Bandit Keith!

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.220
Someone's coming.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.430
Perfect.  He'll be our last prey!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.840
What's with you?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.960
That's a Duel Disk.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:45.460
I see.  You've been taking cards using cheap tricks.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:52.200
What should we do?  We need one more Puzzle Card.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:56.200
Oh, you have five Puzzle Cards?

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.750
I remember you!

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:03.950
You're that flunky who hung out with Yugi at Duelist Kingdom!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:09.950
Oh yeah.  But I've never seen him duel.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.820
He's an amateur.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.460
Okay!  I challenge you to a duel!

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.680
Maybe you shouldn't be so impulsive.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.880
I'm the duelist known as Ghost Kotsuzuka.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.470
I won't lose to an amateur!

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:35.980
I can erase him easily, but this is a good chance to warm up using my Occult Deck.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:37.480
Fine!

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:40.700
But only if we wager all our Puzzle Cards.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.720
I have one.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.120
What?

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.940
How dumb.  Out of the question.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:53.230
Don't you know that over half the slots in the finals are already taken?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.040
What?

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.230
If you waste time, it won't matter how many Puzzle Cards you have.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.200
Whoever wins will make the finals!

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:07.980
Fine!  Feel the horror of my Ghost Deck!

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:11.610
No, you'll learn what real horror is.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.480
Let's begin the Shadow Game!

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.970
It's getting spooky.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.170
Here I go!  My turn!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.440
I draw a card!

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:44.760
Did you know this cemetery has a grave with severed heads?

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.010
Severed heads?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:52.840
Yes.  A headless ghost wanders around here, looking for his head.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.270
What?

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:02.540
Don't you hear the footsteps of a ghost searching for his head?

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:04.800
You're lying!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.500
I summon Headless Knight!

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:15.060
You idiot!  You're not the one supposed to be scared!

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.800
Y-You're right.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.060
I set one card.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.150
I end my turn.  It's your turn.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.660
You didn't scare me.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:29.890
My turn!

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.470
My monster is The Snake Hair!

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.900
1500 attack points!

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:40.560
If you look at The Snake Hair, you turn into stone!

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:41.880
Go, The Snake Hair!

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.860
Stone Blizzard!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.650
You no longer have any monsters.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:01.660
Every time I draw a card, you're one step closer to hell.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.320
I flip over my spell card!

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.660
The Shallow Grave.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:15.900
The Shallow Grave lets us both bring a monster back from our graveyards and play it in defense position.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.960
Headless Knight resurrects!

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:32.900
Kotsuzuka, you don't have a monster card in your graveyard!

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.000
Don't worry!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:39.460
Even though he resurrected a monster, Kotsuzuka's monster has more attack points!

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.130
Are you sure?

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.920
I tribute Headless Knight to summon a higher Level monster.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.430
Come out, The Earl of Demise!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.810
What?  2000 attack points?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.120
Take this!  Malevolent Sword - Night Raid!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.250
Dammit!

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.200
What's wrong with your crooked deck?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.460
Crooked?

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.930
I won't forgive you for insulting my deck!

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:19.150
My turn!

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.700
Come on out, Dragon Zombie!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:27.360
And Premature Burial!

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:39.720
By paying 800 life points, this card lets me bring a monster back from my graveyard.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.150
Next, the spell card Polymerization!

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.960
Come, the strongest monster of the afterlife!

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.840
Great Mammoth of Goldfine!

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:07.440
In this tournament, Fusion Monsters can't attack on the turn that it's summoned.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.480
I'll set a card and end my turn.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:14.200
My Ghost Deck's terror is only getting started.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.910
When you start your next turn...

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.480
It's your turn!

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.050
My turn.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:28.820
Good!  I activate the trap card Skull Invitation!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:37.680
Every time a card goes to the graveyard, Skull Invitation deals its owner 300 points of damage.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:46.690
When your monster is destroyed next turn, my Ghost combo will deal you 300 points of damage!

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:51.220
You can no longer insult my Ghost Deck!

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.220
What's with him?

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.560
He's gone insane because he knows he'll lose.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:07.040
As you wish, if you want me to put my cards into the graveyard, I'll discard my whole hand!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:09.660
What?

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.650
He really did lose his mind.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.380
He self-destructed.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.280
Good.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.820
Go, Skull Invitation!

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:27.130
He's as good as dead!

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.840
What's so funny?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.920
I'm getting excited.

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:39.140
Just imagining how afraid you'll be gives me the shivers.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.900
Haven't you realized yet?

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:45.600
Look at my feet.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:49.650
I activated a spell card before I discarded my hand.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:53.940
That's...

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.880
This spell card is Spiritualistic Medium.

00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:03.660
For every card I discarded this turn, a monster gains 500 attack points.

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:04.660
What?

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.770
I discarded four cards.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:15.670
The grudge from the four cards gives 2000 attack points to The Earl of Demise.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.420
4000 attack points?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.170
Take this!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.350
Big Night Raid!

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.850
My Great Mammoth of Goldfine...

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:41.830
Due to your own trap's effect, you lose 300 life points!

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:50.840
If you don't pull yourself together, you all won't make it out of here alive.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:53.320
What do you mean?

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:55.720
You weren't listening?

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.350
Look around.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:06.700
What are they?

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.960
These grim reapers are coming to meet you.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:13.370
I said this was a Shadow Game.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:17.400
Whoever loses this duel will be dragged to the shadow world.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.200
No way!

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:22.200
Good.  Get more scared!

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:24.980
I love watching people quaking in fear!

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:28.740
I don't want to die!

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:30.480
Takaido!

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.390
Why am I back here?

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.390
Running away is pointless.

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:45.730
No one can escape from a Shadow Game.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:50.240
You have to defeat me if you want to live.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.740
Kotsuzuka!  I won't forgive you if you lose!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:57.340
Yeah!  Don't you dare lose!

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.350
M-My turn...

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:05.350
G-Good.

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:08.350
The spell card Nightmare's Steelcage!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:16.600
All monsters can't attack for two turns.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.300
And I set a monster in defense position!

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:24.420
Kotsuzuka, use this time to improve your situation!

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.300
I know!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.380
My turn.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.140
He didn't draw anything good.

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.820
I wanted to see you suffer more.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.820
But it seems your time is up.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.760
What are you talking about?

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:47.690
As long as I have Nightmare's Steelcage, no monster can attack for two turns!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:52.880
Your trick doesn't work against my Occult Deck!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.820
I activate Ectoplasmer!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:06.710
By turning half the monster's attack points into ectoplasm, it can attack you directly.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.210
What?

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.040
Fire the ectoplasm!

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.800
Too bad.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.770
Time to go to hell.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:30.370
Wander the afterlife forever.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.380
What's this?

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:55.000
Just wait, Yugi and Marik.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:06.270
I wonder if anyone qualified for the finals before us.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:09.000
We won't know until we get there.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.980
That's Kaiba's helicopter.

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:20.990
You slowpokes can follow my footsteps on the road of battle!

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:25.140
Hey!  Kaiba passed us!

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.700
I'm not faster than a helicopter, idiot!

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.990
I'm finally here.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:33.920
Up ahead is the Battle City Finals.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:46.380
As we head towards the final venue, the Hollywood star Jean-Claude Magnum arrives.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.750
He was waiting so that he could propose to Mai?

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:54.890
Mai ignores him, so he challenges her to a duel.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.420
If he wins, she has to marry him?

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.720
There's no way she'll accept-

00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:02.390
What?  Mai accepts?

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.070
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Meet Ninja Master Magnum

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:07.660
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:26.230
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:31.600
I feel like I've been here

00:22:32.130 --> 00:22:41.260
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:52.770
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.660 --> 00:23:00.300
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:05.570
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:10.650
Will never change

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:15.950
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:21.150
To be who I am

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:26.390
I've kept searching for something

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:31.070
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:34.030
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:41.140
From now until forever...
